{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:fbfbe56404490aab","name":"The Last Resort","source":{"id":"source:reference-fbfbe56404490aab","title":"The Last Resort","revision":24872,"timestamp":"2024-11-07T18:17:19Z","sha256":"af8f5f4299533d474ee095936ad48ec7ee0d0ae997467e99a7649c11ba053747","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24872","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Last%20Resort&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-fbfbe56404490aab","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Last Resort"]}," is the home, workshop, and laboratory of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gorman Vandrayk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gorman_Vandrayk?action=edit&redlink=1"},", better known as \"Camper.\" Never a first-class ship, even when it was a new Amalgamated Hyperdyne ",{"tag":"a","children":["578-R Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/578-R_Space_Transport","referenceId":"reference:714de75c47b4e1cb"},", The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Last Resort"]}," deteriorates even further as it sits idle on the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Taris"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Taris","referenceId":"reference:6c77edc098cd2a27"},". Camper is hiding on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Taris"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Taris","referenceId":"reference:6c77edc098cd2a27"}," from his former employers, and he is willing to let a collection of tents and awnings conceal the ship, obscuring its true form. He tinkers with some systems, such as configuring a powerful cannon at the expense of his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," and shields, and he neglects others completely. The cargo deck level becomes his workshop, housin